    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d226">

                <pb facs="0333" n="317" sameAs="frus:frus1948v09/pg317"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">835.20/5–1348: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bowers</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">us urgent</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-05-13T13:00:00-04:00">May 13, 1948—1 p.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>308. Vergara<anchor n="1" xml:id="d226-f1"/> says Chile and especially Chilean
                    Army much interested in the rather remarkably large military mission from
                    Argentina headed by Minister of War<anchor n="2" xml:id="d226-f2"/> going to
                    Washington. It is thought here that purpose is to acquire great amount military
                    equipment and probably to get assistance in the building and expansion of arms
                    factories in Argentine. Should this develop the economic effect on Chile will be
                    serious since the armed forces here would demand heavy <pb facs="0334" n="318"
                        xml:id="pg318"/> appropriations to meet resulting danger from Argentina.
                    Vergara thinks most South American countries would be concerned over our
                    assistance in building up a powerful military machine by Perón.<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d226-f3"/>
                </p>
                <p>Vergara asks if we can give him any reassurance as to purpose of Argentine
                    mission and as to our disposition. (Comment.) I know that when General
                        Crittenberger<anchor n="4" xml:id="d226-f4"/> spent about ten days in Buenos
                    Aires in close contact with Argentine Army and passing through Chile stayed a
                    little more than a day there was much speculation here as to significance and
                    this followed by the Argentine mission to Washington has not unnaturally created
                    serious concern. Anything we may be able to report to Vergara would be
                    appreciated by Embassy.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bowers</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
